    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "subjective",
      "section": "Section C",
      "marks": 3,
      "question": "Find the middle term in the expansion of $(\\frac{x}{3} + 9y)^{10}$.",
      "finalAnswer": "$61236 x^5 y^5$",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "$n=10$, middle term is $T_6$.",
        "$T_6 = ^{10}C_5 (\\frac{x}{3})^5 (9y)^5$.",
        "$252 \\cdot \\frac{x^5}{3^5} \\cdot 9^5 y^5 = 252 \\cdot x^5 y^5 \\cdot \\frac{(3^2)^5}{3^5}$.",
        "$252 \\cdot 3^5 \\cdot x^5 y^5 = 252 \\cdot 243 \\cdot x^5 y^5 = 61236 x^5 y^5$."
      ]
